From 6b4d55b20affb3744492738498fe4cdd92fc83c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 19:41:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] A per-case timeout: a forked body that hangs is killed, and
 the hang shrinks

An infinite loop or a deadlock in the code under test hung the run: the
fork parent blocked in read() on the child's request pipe, and a
HEGEL_ISOLATED block's parent on its verdict pipe, both for ever.  Hangs
are a bug class the kernel harnesses can reach, and a hung run reports
nothing.

A forked body now has a deadline.  The parent reads its pipe through
hegel__read_deadline (poll with the time left on the monotonic clock);
when the deadline passes first it SIGKILLs the child and the case ends
INTERESTING, like a crash:

  fork mode       origin "timeout",
                  "test case timed out after N ms (killed)"
  HEGEL_ISOLATED  the block's origin (one block = one bug, so a bug that
                  hangs on some inputs and crashes on others shrinks as
                  one), "HEGEL_ISOLATED block at <site> timed out ..."

hegel_run_options gets timeout_ms: 0 is HEGEL_DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_MS (10 s),
HEGEL_OFF is no deadline.  HEGEL_C_TIMEOUT_MS in the environment
overrides it (0 = none): like HEGEL_C_FORK the environment wins, so a
slow machine, an ASan build or a debugger needs no rebuild.

On by default, so behaviour changes: a case that honestly takes more
than 10 s of wall time under a fork runner (engine time serving its draws
included) is now a failure.  Candidates to check: MPI spawn tests, ASan
kernel harnesses, fork-clean mode, and fork-mode repeat loops that run to
the choice budget (TODO.md says those already trip TooSlow).

Known limits, documented in hegel_c.h: every hanging execution costs the
whole timeout, so shrinking a hang at the default is slow (the selftest
uses 300 ms); a case near the deadline replays nondeterministically; only
the forked body is killed, not processes it started; nofork code outside
a block has no deadline.

tests/selftest/test_timeout_hang.c (TESTS_SHRINK): a ring walk that never
ends when its step is a multiple of 8, under fork and under nofork +
HEGEL_ISOLATED; both must shrink to step 8.

Not built or run: written in a sandbox that could not build the
repository (gcc -fsyntax-only -Wall -Wextra is clean on the changed
files).  Run make test, then the Scotch, MPI and Linux pins, before
keeping it.

